		<title type="html"><![CDATA[New OpenGD77 CPS 2024 12 07]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4644&amp;p=34491#p34491"><![CDATA[
A new version of the OpenGD77CPS is available<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/PC_CPS/Latest/" class="postlink">downloads/PC_CPS/Latest/</a><br><br>Specifically<br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/PC_CPS/Latest/OpenGD77CPSInstaller_R2024.12.07.01.exe" class="postlink">downloads/PC_CPS/Latest/OpenGD77CPSInst ... .07.01.exe</a><br><br><br>This version has a small change to the calibration screen so that it automatically prompts to save the calibration data to a file for non-GD77 radios.<br>This change was made because the CPS only supports adjusting the calibration data for GD-77 type radios, and the previous user interface didn't make it clear that the only think that it can do for non GD-77 radios is load and save data after its been read from the radio<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Dec 07, 2024 9:44 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
